.TH PLICAD-LIB 7
.SH NAME
plicad-lib \- the library of PliCad and the layout of its tree
.SH DESCRIPTION
The tree of PliCad holds:
.TP 12
.B src/
every program, side by side;
.TP
.B man/
the manual pages: man1 for the programs, man5 for the files, man7 for
the language,
.IR plicad (7),
and this page;
.TP
.B lib/
the library;
.TP
.B test/
the fixtures of the tests and what they expect;
.TP
.B build/
what the build makes.
.PP
A program looks for a file that a source names, as
.B materials
or
.BR template ,
next to that source first, and then in the library: the directory
lib under the directory that PLICAD names, or else the lib of the tree
it was built in.
.SS The library
.TP 12
.B materials
the materials and finishes,
.IR plicad (7):
bodies with their densities, the coats of sheet metal, and the
textures of molds by their VDI 3400 grade with the least draft each
needs, their color unused, as a texture shows that of the body;
.TP
.B templates/
the papers of drawings,
.IR draw (5),
as plain_b.ps, plain_c.ps and plain_d.ps;
.TP
.B tables/
standard tables in plain text, one row a line, a comment at the top
that names the columns: screws (heads and threads by size and style),
holes (clearance holes and countersinks by screw size), inserts
(self-clinching hardware: its kind, its mounting hole, least sheet and
least distance to an edge or a bend line, its thread, the size of its
body and the material of the body, and whether it sits flush in its
hole or in a blind hole of a depth,
.BR "insert " in
.IR sm (5);
a table inserts next to a source adds its types to these),
bends (inside radius and K-factor by material and
thickness) and packages (the bodies of electronic packages);
.TP
.B parts/
bought 3D parts, as
.IB maker / partnumber .part ,
named by their maker and its part number, or
.IB maker / partnumber _ piece .sm
for each piece of one of sheet: sunon/EEC0252B3-000U-A99.part, an axial
fan of 120 mm, and keystone/8353_mount.sm and 8353_strap.sm, the end
mount and the strap of a carry handle;
.TP
.B symbols/
the symbols of schematics;
.TP
.B fonts/
the fonts of the lettering: osifont-lgpl3fe.ttf and osifont-italic.ttf,
the lettering of drawings, whose widths
.IR smsheet (1)
lays text out by, under the license osifont.license (the GPL with the
font exception), for Ghostscript as
.BR "ps2pdf \-sFONTPATH=" $PLICAD/lib/fonts ;
and the glyphs of Nimbus Sans, nimbussans.txt, of the schematics
(nimbussans.LICENSE).
.PP
Screws, inserts and the bodies of packages are families: a part is
made from a row of its table, not kept as a file for each size.
Every length of a table is in the units of
.IR plicad (7),
mm unless a number ends in in.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PLICAD
the directory whose lib is the library.
.SH SEE ALSO
plicad(7), draw(5), sm(5), part(5), assembly(5)
